{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"agent_message","text":"Research execution is complete.\n\nKey result: perfect isolation was achieved only through a literal string-keyed router. The best parameter edit—LoRA with disjoint paraphrase and locality rehearsal—reached:\n\n- 100% exact and held-out semantic success\n- 98.66% accuracy on 224 held-out sums\n- 100% unrelated-control accuracy\n- 33.3% logical portability\n- 5.1% locality generation flips\n\nLeakage was structured: gradient similarity predicted next-token drift (`ρ=0.769`). Unregularized LoRA preserved only 4.32% of held-out sums, while restricting edits to four layers preserved 2.83%.\n\nDeliverables:\n\n- [REPORT.md](/workspaces/isolating-knowledge-updates-bcb6-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/REPORT.md)\n- [README.md](/workspaces/isolating-knowledge-updates-bcb6-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/README.md)\n- [planning.md](/workspaces/isolating-knowledge-updates-bcb6-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/planning.md)\n- [Experiment code](/workspaces/isolating-knowledge-updates-bcb6-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/src/run_experiment.py)\n- [Statistical results](/workspaces/isolating-knowledge-updates-bcb6-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/results/analysis/condition_summary.csv)\n- [Validation record](/workspaces/isolating-knowledge-updates-bcb6-codex-gpt-5-6-sol/results/validation.json)\n\nValidation passed: 14 raw result files × 289 prompts, byte-identical analysis rerun, identical saved-adapter generations, zero log-probability discrepancy, and a clean dependency check. The critical-analysis framework limits the broader evidence rating to low because only one 1.5B model was tested."}}
